'''''Solanum chenopodioides''''', commonly known as the '''whitetip nightshade''' or '''velvety nightshade''', is a shrub of the family [[Solanaceae]] native to South America. It has become naturalised in North America, Europe, Australia, and New Zealand.<ref>{{cite web |url= https://flora.sa.gov.au/taxon/40370-solanum-chenopodioides |title= Solanum chenopodioides Lam., in (ed.), Flora SA. Board of Botanic Gardens and State Herbarium: Adelaide |website= Flora SA. Board of Botanic Gardens and State Herbarium: Adelaide |publisher= Government of South Australia}}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal|last=Guillén Boland|first=Diego Alejandro|date=2015-09-25|title=El erotismo y la ciudad en la poesía de Luis García Montero|journal=Revista de Filología Románica|doi=10.5209/rev_rfrm.2015.49317|issn=1988-2815|doi-access=free}}</ref>

